(Bug #78: a size the compiler cannot see - here it arrives on the command
 line - reached mmap unchecked. 4611686018427387904 bytes is more than any
 mapping can serve, so the allocation answered nothing at all, the nothing
 was stored as the buffer, and the next read of it segfaulted. The bound
 is now held at run time too: the buffer is made with no capacity, the
 error flag is raised so `On error` can catch it, and the program carries
 on - the truncation behaviour the manual gives every full fixed buffer.)

a number called wanted is arguments's first as a number.
a buffer called room is wanted bytes in size.
On error print "that size was refused".

Print "capacity: {room's capacity}".
Set room to "hello".
Print "size after writing: {room's size}".
Print "full: {room's full}".
